         be derived from $(MSBuildProgramFiles32), which on a 64-bit install resolves to
         "C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\...", a path that does not exist.
         Every import guarded by Exists('$(VSToolsPath)\...') was therefore skipped, including
         Microsoft.Web.Publishing.targets, so Web.Debug.config / Web.Release.config were never
         transformed and a Release deploy shipped the base Web.config. Try each known layout. -->
    <!-- Visual Studio 2026 / MSBuild 18 -->
    <VSToolsPath Condition="'$(VSToolsPath)'=='' And Exists('$(MSBuildExtensionsPath)\Microsoft\VisualStudio\v18.0')">$(MSBuildExtensionsPath)\Microsoft\VisualStudio\v18.0</VSToolsPath>
